message: "If you use Semaprax, cite this repository state and the exact evidence document that supports your claim."
title: "Semaprax"
type: software
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: 2026-09-02
abstract: "Semaprax is an experimental agent-native systems programming language built around a stable semantic program graph. Its v0.2 prototype lets coding agents query typed meaning, submit revision-bound semantic patches, and lower a verified subset to native executables and browser/Wasm packages."
authors:
  - name: "Wavect GmbH"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wavect/semaprax"
url: "https://wavect.io/semaprax/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - agent-native programming language
  - systems programming
  - semantic program graph
  - semantic patches
  - WebAssembly
